# INERT ON GITHUB PAGES. This file does nothing today.
#
# asylumstats.co.uk is served by GitHub Pages (`server: GitHub.com`), which ignores
# `_headers`. That is a Cloudflare Pages and Netlify convention. So none of the headers
# below currently reach a browser: no HSTS, no X-Frame-Options, no nosniff, no
# Referrer-Policy, no Permissions-Policy. The only policy in force is the meta CSP in
# src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro, and `frame-ancestors` is ignored by spec when delivered
# via <meta>, so the site has no clickjacking protection at all.
#
# It is kept, not deleted, because it is the whole configuration needed if the site moves
# to Cloudflare Pages, which is the fix for the missing headers.
#
# The CSP here MUST stay in step with the meta CSP in BaseLayout.astro. When both are
# present a browser enforces the intersection, so a directive missing here silently
# becomes a block. It had already drifted: `connect-src` here omitted
# https://api.postcodes.io, which the homepage postcode lookup calls. That works today
# only because this file is inert; on the first Cloudflare deploy the site's primary
# call to action would have stopped working with no code change to explain it. Now
# synced.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.postcodes.io https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
